					<!-- Work 6 -->
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-zinc-950/70 border border-zinc-800 hover:border-amber-600/50 transition">
						<div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-mono text-zinc-500 mb-1.5">
							<span>THEATRE COMIC · 2012</span>
							<span class="text-amber-400 font-bold">06</span>
						</div>
						<h3 class="text-base font-bold font-serif text-white mb-2">Antigonick</h3>
						<p class="text-xs text-zinc-300/90 leading-relaxed">
							<span class="lang-zh">以手写墨字与半透明画页重述索福克勒斯的《安提戈涅》，将时间度量者具象化置于舞台角落，重构抗争与埋葬礼仪的张力。</span>
							<span class="lang-en">A visual reinvention of Sophocles where handwritten script and transparent overlays interrogate tyranny, burial rites, and the crushing pace of time.</span>
						</p>
					</div>

					<!-- Work 7 -->
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-zinc-950/70 border border-zinc-800 hover:border-amber-600/50 transition">
						<div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-mono text-zinc-500 mb-1.5">
							<span>DRAMA POEM · 2019</span>
							<span class="text-amber-400 font-bold">07</span>
						</div>
						<h3 class="text-base font-bold font-serif text-white mb-2">Norma Jeane Baker of Troy</h3>
						<p class="text-xs text-zinc-300/90 leading-relaxed">
							<span class="lang-zh">将好莱坞巨星玛丽莲·梦露与特洛伊海伦的神话命运交织重叠，在打字机机械敲击声中追问女性美貌如何被权力与战争机器消费。</span>
							<span class="lang-en">A poetic play interweaving Marilyn Monroe with Helen of Troy, interrogating how mythology and warfare commodify female beauty.</span>
						</p>
					</div>
